}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1b08d935-e1fb-5247-a1f0-f1700cf91e07"],

Cell["\<\
A Hypergraph draws itself by default, the way a Graph does, so HypergraphPlot \
is needed only in order to pass options.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"95b75294-86d8-d84d-96f4-ae0ca6ca3680"],

Cell["Arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ee5e3514-8cc1-2e49-8835-14b33eb8c259"],

Cell["\<\
An array is a nesting of lists, and one object holds any of them: nothing \
about the structure of an array depends on what sits in its entries, which \
may be numbers, elements of a finite field, symbolic expressions or labels. \
The order of an array is its number of indices, and an array of order n is an \
n-array: a vector is a 1-array and a matrix is a 2-array. A scalar is the \
0-array. An array is regular when all of its indices range over the same \
length, and only a regular array can carry an index symmetry.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bb65972a-9597-9d46-b584-1060183402db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "What an array is made of is read off its entries by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayDomain", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9df4d661-2000-a54e-99ca-48bf4b88a7a4"],
 " rather than declared alongside them. The symmetry is the one thing it is \
told rather than asked, being a claim about the entries that they may or may \
not bear out."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4809e366-ac4b-6748-a100-93bdf9a28a10"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayObject", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "67d0aa72-6db1-7445-be18-8b432a457e58"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an array, whatever its entries are"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b25efd73-d628-7243-a2fe-071df98c18ff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["GenerateSymbolicArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"818e523f-a3f2-fc45-bd4d-b452fd93c58c"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "build one whose entries are a name applied to the indices"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c86479d9-e6aa-4f4c-bd6d-5a5fb7b9170a"],

Cell[TextData[{
